Build Facility Geometry — Bike
Bike facilities are line geometry, buffered directly: utah_bikeways’s Facility1 field distinguishes facility type, and "Not Available" is the only value that means no bike facility, so everything else – on-street bike lanes and trails alike – is existing network. The 2055 vintage adds the RTP 2027 Preferred Scenario’s active-transportation projects as-is.


Show the code
bike_raw = {
    2027: gpd.read_file(
        L["utah_bikeways"], where="Facility1 IS NOT NULL AND Facility1 &lt;&gt; 'Not Available'"
    ).to_crs(CRS)[["geometry"]],
    2032: gpd.GeoDataFrame(geometry=[], crs=CRS),  # placeholder: 2032 bike layer TBD
    2055: gpd.GeoDataFrame(
        pd.concat(
            [
                gpd.read_file(L["at_line_projects"]).to_crs(CRS)[["geometry"]],
                gpd.read_file(L["at_point_projects"]).to_crs(CRS)[["geometry"]],
            ],
            ignore_index=True,
        ),
        geometry="geometry",
        crs=CRS,
    ),
}
for year, gdf in bike_raw.items():
    print(f"Bike {year} adds: {len(gdf)} features")


Bike 2027 adds: 17316 features
Bike 2032 adds: 0 features
Bike 2055 adds: 866 features


Each vintage’s cumulative network is its own adds plus everything the vintage it builds_on already had – so a vintage with nothing new yet (2032, for now) is simply identical to the vintage beneath it, not empty. Buffering and dissolving that cumulative network once per vintage gives the geometry every scenario needing that vintage can reuse.


Show the code
bike_cum = {}
for year in sorted(GIS_VINTAGES["bike"]):
    builds_on = GIS_VINTAGES["bike"][year]["builds_on"]
    parts = [bike_raw[year]] if builds_on is None else [bike_cum[builds_on], bike_raw[year]]
    bike_cum[year] = gpd.GeoDataFrame(pd.concat(parts, ignore_index=True), geometry="geometry", crs=CRS)

bike_buffers = {
    year: gpd.GeoDataFrame(geometry=[cum.buffer(CONSTANTS["buffer_m"]).union_all()], crs=CRS)
    for year, cum in bike_cum.items()
}
for year, cum in bike_cum.items():
    print(f"Bike {year} cumulative: {len(cum)} features")


Bike 2027 cumulative: 17316 features
Bike 2032 cumulative: 17316 features
Bike 2055 cumulative: 18182 features
